@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "TermsAndConditions";
    Layout = "~/Views/Shared/_Layout.cshtml";
}



<div class="container py-5">
    <div class="row justify-content-center">
        <div class="col-lg-10">
            <div class="bg-light p-4 rounded shadow-sm">
                <h2 class="mb-4 text-center text-primary">Terms and Conditions</h2>

                <h5 class="mt-4 text-dark">1. Definitions</h5>
                <ul class="text-dark">
                    <li><strong>Acceptance Form:</strong> The form provided by the School for parents to accept a place for their child.</li>
                    <li><strong>Behavior Policy:</strong> School policy on conduct expectations.</li>
                    <li><strong>Child:</strong> Any student admitted to Iqra Educational Institute.</li>
                    <li><strong>Complaints Procedure:</strong> Official process for handling parental complaints.</li>
                    <li><strong>Deposit:</strong> The amount defined in the Acceptance Form and Schedule of Fees.</li>
                    <li><strong>Fees:</strong> Tuition and charges listed on the website and fee schedule.</li>
                    <li><strong>Head of School:</strong> The individual appointed to oversee school operations.</li>
                    <li><strong>Schedule of Fees:</strong> Official list of applicable school charges.</li>
                    <li><strong>Term:</strong> One academic session as defined by the school calendar.</li>
                    <li><strong>Term’s Notice:</strong> Written notification provided before a student leaves.</li>
                    <li><strong>We / School:</strong> Refers to Iqra Educational Institute.</li>
                    <li><strong>You / Parents:</strong> Those who have signed the Acceptance Form or equivalent.</li>
                </ul>

                <h5 class="mt-4 text-dark">2. Notice Requirements</h5>
                <ul class="text-dark">
                    <li>Parents must provide a term’s notice or pay a term’s fees if withdrawing a child early.</li>
                    <li>Fees in lieu of notice become payable on the first day of what would’ve been the last term.</li>
                    <li>Half-term notice is required to withdraw from supplemental activities or charges apply.</li>
                    <li>Mid-term withdrawals do not qualify for fee reduction or refund.</li>
                </ul>

                <h5 class="mt-4 text-dark">3. Behavior Policy</h5>
                <p class="text-dark">All students must comply with the school’s Behavior Policy and maintain punctual attendance.</p>

                <h5 class="mt-4 text-dark">4. Suspension and Required Removal</h5>
                <p class="text-dark">The Head of School has the authority to suspend or remove a student in cases of serious or persistent misconduct.</p>

                <h5 class="mt-4 text-dark">5. The School’s Obligations</h5>
                <ul class="text-dark">
                    <li>The school is not responsible if a child cannot complete schooling due to lack of ability.</li>
                    <li>We commit to reasonable care and quality of education during the student’s enrollment.</li>
                    <li>Urgent medical decisions may be taken by the school if parental consent cannot be obtained in time.</li>
                    <li>Progress will be monitored and communicated; diagnosis of learning disorders is not guaranteed.</li>
                    <li>Parental cooperation is essential for fulfilling school responsibilities.</li>
                </ul>

                <h5 class="mt-4 text-dark">6. The Parents’ Obligations</h5>
                <ul class="text-dark">
                    <li>Maintain a positive relationship with school staff and support your child’s education at home.</li>
                    <li>Keep the school updated on important changes related to the student or finances.</li>
                    <li>Inform the school of absences in writing and in advance where possible.</li>
                    <li>The school is not responsible for students off-campus unless part of a school activity.</li>
                    <li>Concerns must be reported promptly using the Complaints Procedure.</li>
                </ul>

                <h5 class="mt-4 text-dark">7. Communications</h5>
                <ul class="text-dark">
                    <li>All official communication must be written.</li>
                    <li>Parents must notify the school of any change in contact details.</li>
                    <li>Notices must be addressed to the Head of School and delivered in a verifiable way.</li>
                </ul>

                <h5 class="mt-4 text-dark">8. Claims against the School</h5>
                <ul class="text-dark">
                    <li>Any liability is limited to the insurance cover available at that time.</li>
                    <li>Only signatories to this agreement can make claims; no third-party rights are included.</li>
                </ul>

                <h5 class="mt-4 text-dark">9. Interpretation</h5>
                <p class="text-dark">Section headings are for reference only and are not legally binding parts of the agreement.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>


